      "value": "@{5a49664b513e7625f7f9509e|full_name}: I still think it's a non-issue having to hide and show your friends avatars if the instance gets busy. If you manually show your friends very poor avatar in the first place then that's on you. Creating a whole new system to deal with your decision does not make sense to me.\nI strongly disagree with making poor avatars unavailable in certain instances would in any way \"encourage\" people to use better ones. They would most likely just get angry and leave the instance all together because avatars matter a lot to people, they want to be \"themselves\".\nHowever if they joined a instance and saw indicators that the majority of people have their avatar hidden, and people sticking to their guns and refusing to manually show others poor avatars then I think the message of \"letting people know that their bad performing avatar is not welcome\" comes across much better.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
